<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul prosecutors said to probe share manipulation.</title>
<headline>Seoul prosecutors said to probe share manipulation.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Securities Exchange Commission (SEC) has asked local prosecutors to investigate incidents of alleged stock price manipulation and insider trading, market watchers said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;There are three cases of manipulation that will be turned over for the prosecutor's office to handle,&quot; said a local broker who asked not to be named.</p>
<p>The SEC declined to comment.</p>
<p>&quot;This investigation could put a damper on the market in the short-term. Large-cap shares are in the process of correction and investors may become more careful of small-caps,&quot; said Steven Lee, a market analyst at Shinyoung Securities.</p>
<p>After eight consecutive days of gains, the stock market closed down 13.67 points at 828.61 on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
